From c20af2ab0114cb561dba9c86b5cd34c2805a65bc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Z User <z@container>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 14:57:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] a11y(ui): announce error toasts with role=alert and assertive
 live region
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

All toasts previously used role="status" inside an aria-live="polite"
container. Polite live regions let screen readers finish whatever they're
saying before announcing the new content — fine for success/info toasts,
but error notifications ("No se pudo guardar…", "Sesión expirada", etc.)
should interrupt the user immediately so they know something went wrong.

Use role="alert" + aria-live="assertive" for error toasts; keep
role="status" + polite for the rest. The container's aria-live is kept
as a fallback; the per-toast role+aria-live takes precedence per the
ARIA spec.
---
 src/lib/components/Toast.svelte | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/lib/components/Toast.svelte b/src/lib/components/Toast.svelte
index c73a76f..ff60e5e 100644
--- a/src/lib/components/Toast.svelte
+++ b/src/lib/components/Toast.svelte
@@ -46,7 +46,8 @@
 			class="pointer-events-auto flex items-start gap-3 rounded-xl border bg-surface shadow-lg px-4 py-3 {styles[
 				t.type
 			].border}"
-			role="status"
+			role={t.type === 'error' ? 'alert' : 'status'}
+			aria-live={t.type === 'error' ? 'assertive' : 'polite'}
 		>
 			<span
 				class="w-7 h-7 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center shrink-0 {styles[t.type].icon}"
-- 
